# Meridian event network — hosts-file fallback.
#
# When Meridian does not control the network's DNS, browser and PWA access is not
# guaranteed and the installed Capacitor app is the reliable client (technical
# spec 8.2 rule 4, 8.4). This file is the narrow middle case: a small number of
# machines that must reach the node in a browser, on a network whose DNS you
# cannot change.
#
# It is a per-machine edit, so it does not scale to a staff roster and is not the
# on-site plan. Use deploy/dns/onsite-dnsmasq.conf on a Meridian-controlled router
# for that.
#
# Append to:
#   Linux, macOS   /etc/hosts
#   Windows        C:\Windows\System32\drivers\etc\hosts
#
# The name must be the one on the node's certificate. Pointing a different name at
# the node produces a certificate warning, and clicking through it is God-mode and
# emergency access only, never normal staff workflow (technical spec 8.2 rule 6).
#
# Replace the address and hostname; both are fake.

10.10.0.2	juplaya-2027-onsite.example.org
